{
  "about": "What a repeating order takes back from a person's own days (spec/sync-protocol.md, Repeating orders). givesWay: when orders are taken with clear_from `from` at `clock`, a stored value gives way (is cleared) when it is a PATTERN, START or END, on or after `from`, set at a clock older than the orders' (HLC order, spec/vectors/hlc.json); memos and people stay. Devices apply it when they start a new job's order themselves. heldBackBy (the server alone, which keeps every clear it made as a floor): an edit arriving later is held back when some floor would have cleared it, and answered with that clear under the floor's clock; `expected` is the `from` of the newest such floor, or null when the edit is taken. Fields are DayField names without the DAY_FIELD_ prefix.",
  "givesWay": [
    {
      "name": "a pattern set before the orders, from their start",
      "floor": {
        "from": "2026-10-03",
        "clock": {
          "ms": 2000,
          "counter": 1,
          "device": "phone"
        }
      },
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "field": "PATTERN",
      "set": {
        "ms": 1000,
        "counter": 0,
        "device": "phone"
      },
      "expected": true
    },
    {
      "name": "a time too",
      "floor": {
        "from": "2026-10-03",
        "clock": {
          "ms": 2000,
          "counter": 1,
          "device": "phone"
        }
      },
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "field": "START",
      "set": {
        "ms": 1000,
        "counter": 0,
        "device": "phone"
      },
      "expected": true
    },
    {
